{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because relaxed blues-rock is what I want to hear today.",
    "Step Back and Let Me Get By connect with the blues guitar interest reflected in People, Hell & Angels, while Croz and Plain Spoken appeal to the songwriting side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Heaven & Earth misses my current interest because progressive rock does not offer the blues and roots sound I am seeking today.",
    "The Endless River's atmospheric, largely instrumental direction feels less relevant when I want songs and blues guitar."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to stretch my interest in guitar-led rock into a broader interest in progressive and atmospheric rock.",
    "A familiar rock connection alone is not enough to make me choose an album; Led Zeppelin feels broadly relevant, but the title gives me little reason to prefer it over The Breeze."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The relaxed blues connection to Old Sock matters more to my choice today than a general connection to rock.",
    "My interest in Blown Away makes country a reasonable suggestion, but it does not mean country is what I want on this visit; I am choosing just one album and leaning toward blues."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in blues, roots music and songwriting, but extend it too broadly into rock that does not fit my mood today."
}"}
